   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Factory6G Simulation Results Report
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,920:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Generated: 2026-03-27
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,921:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Executive Summary
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,922:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This report presents a comprehensive evaluation of the Factory6G physical layer simulation platform, covering 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,923:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: six
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: channel estimation methods
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: three modulation schemes
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: three channel models
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,925:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: three factory sizes
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,926:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , and the 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,926:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: JIDD-SCMA
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,926:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  joint detection-decoding system. All experiments were conducted in March 2026.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Key findings:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Adaptive and PSO
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  channel estimators achieve the lowest BER floors (~3-4 x 10^-5), an order of
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: magnitude better than LS (~3 x 10^-4). PSO is 14x slower than Adaptive for comparable
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: performance.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,932:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,932:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: JIDD-SCMA
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  achieves effectively zero BER above 9 dB Eb/N0, demonstrating the power of joint
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: iterative detection-decoding, but at 162x the computational cost of LS.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Neural estimator
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  produces BER identical to LS -- it has not learned beyond the baseline.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Higher-order modulation
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (64-QAM) raises the BER floor to ~1.1 x 10^-2 and triples latency
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: compared to QPSK.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rayleigh fading
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is the easiest channel (zero BER above 8 dB with LS), while 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: TR 38.901 UMi
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: produces a persistent BER floor (~3 x 10^-4).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,939:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Large factory environments
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,940:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (40x40 m) cause severe multipath degradation with BER stuck at
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ~0.21 -- current estimation methods cannot cope.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: A critical 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,941:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: numerical bug
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,942:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  in JIDD-SCMA Run 1 caused BER to rebound to 0.5 at high SNR; this
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,943:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: was fixed in Run 2.
