   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Analysis:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:20,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Adaptive and PSO are the top performers
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,006:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , both achieving BER floors of ~3-4 x 10^-5 -- roughly
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,010:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10x lower than LS. At 12 dB, Adaptive edges ahead (2.94e-5 vs 3.75e-5), but the difference is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,011:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: within noise. PSO reaches its floor faster at low SNR (4.79e-3 at 0 dB vs 2.42e-2 for LS), suggesting
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,011:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: better noise resilience.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,012:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,012:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: LS and Neural produce identical BER
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,015:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  at every Eb/N0 point. The neural estimator has collapsed to
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the LS solution and provides no benefit over the baseline. This likely indicates insufficient training
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: data diversity or model capacity.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,017:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ISTA
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,020:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  starts poorly at low SNR (0.395 at 0 dB) but converges to ~3.3 x 10^-4 at 20 dB, comparable
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to LS. Its iterative shrinkage approach needs a minimum SNR threshold (~8 dB) before becoming
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: competitive.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,022:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,022:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DFT
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  has the worst BER floor (~4-8 x 10^-3) and actually degrades at higher SNR (rising from
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,025:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.5e-3 at 10 dB to 7.8e-3 at 20 dB). Note: the medium factory comparison is not fully fair.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,026:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,026:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All methods except JIDD-SCMA exhibit a 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,026:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BER floor
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , indicating channel estimation error
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,027:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dominates over noise at high SNR.
