   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Total bits tested | 71.8M | 621M |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 8 dB | 6.1e-6 | 6.1e-6 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 10 dB |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.6e-3 | 2.8e-7 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 13 dB | 0.486 | 0 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 20 dB | 0.500 | 0 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Run 1
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  had a critical numerical bug: BER drops normally through the waterfall region (1-9 dB), reaches zero at 9 dB,
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but then 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: rebounds to ~0.5
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  from 10-20 dB. A BER of 0.5 means random guessing -- the decoder output is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: uncorrelated with the input. Root cause: the log-likelihood computation 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: f = -(1/N0) * |y - signal|^2
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: overflows when N0 approaches zero at high SNR.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Run 2
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  resolved this: BER drops monotonically and remains at 0 above 9 dB. Each high-SNR point was tested with
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 50M bits, confirming BER 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6e-8 (upper bound).
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7.2 JIDD-SCMA Waterfall Performance (Run 2)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,196:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Eb/N0 (dB) | BER | Bit Errors | Total Bits |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |---|---|---|---|
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 1 | 0.474 | 24,045 | 50,688 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 3 | 0.440 | 22,286 | 50,688 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5 | 0.090 | 4,557 | 50,688 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 6 | 2.94e-3 | 149 | 50,688 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 7 | 1.41e-4 | 128 | 907,008 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 8 | 6.10e-6 | 122 | 19,987,968 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9 | 0 | 0 | 50,000,640 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 10 | 2.80e-7 | 14 | 50,000,640 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 12-20 | 0 | 0 | 50,000,640 each |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The waterfall region spans 5-8 dB with BER dropping 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5 orders of magnitude in 3 dB
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . This steep slope is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: characteristic of the joint iterative processing where the polar code SCAN decoder and SCMA MPA detector
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reinforce each other through message passing.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. Cross-System Comparison
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8.1 BER Comparison
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /app/reports/plots/combined_ber.png, 1295, 829
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Aspect | LS (baseline) | Adaptive | PSO | JIDD-SCMA |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |---|---|---|---|---|
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 6 dB | 4.6e-4 | 7.8e-5 | 8.5e-5 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,221:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.9e-3 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 8 dB | 3.5e-4 | 5.1e-5 | 4.9e-5 | 6.1e-6 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER at 10 dB | 3.0e-4 | 4.4e-5 | 4.7e-5 | ~0 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,222:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,223:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | BER floor |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,223:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ~3e-4 | ~3e-5 | ~4e-5 | 0 (within 50M bits) |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Architecture | OFDM+LDPC | OFDM+LDPC | OFDM+LDPC |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,224:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SCMA+Polar+JIDD |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Key observations:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: JIDD-SCMA achieves the lowest absolute BER
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,230:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  at moderate-to-high SNR, reaching effectively
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: zero errors above 9 dB. However, it has the worst BER below 6 dB because the SCMA system is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: designed for the multi-user overloaded regime rather than low-SNR operation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,232:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Adaptive and PSO
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,233:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  provide the best BER among OFDM-based methods but still have an error floor
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that JIDD-SCMA does not exhibit.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The two system types are 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,234:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: not directly comparable
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,236:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -- different modulation, coding, and multiple
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,237:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: access. But the comparison illustrates the BER advantage of joint processing vs. separate
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,237:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimation-then-decoding.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,237:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8.2 Runtime Comparison
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,238:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /app/reports/plots/runtime_comparison.png, 1446, 716
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Method | Total Runtime | Relative to LS |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |---|---|---|
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | ISTA | 91.7 s | 0.11x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | DFT | 96.5 s | 0.12x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | LS | 817.7 s |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.0x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Neural | 817.4 s | 1.0x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Adaptive | 5,838 s (1.6 h) | 7.1x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | JIDD Run 1 | 20,615 s (5.7 h) | 25x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | PSO |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 82,703 s (23.0 h) | 101x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | JIDD Run 2 | 132,460 s (36.8 h) | 162x |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,254:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: JIDD Run 2 is expensive primarily because it tests 50M bits per high-SNR point to confirm zero errors. The
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,254:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: per-frame cost of JIDD (iterative MPA+SCAN) is also inherently higher than single-pass estimation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. Summary of Findings
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | # | Finding | Impact |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |---|---|---|
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 1 | Adaptive is the best estimator (BER ~3e-5) | Default choice for OFDM pipeline
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,257:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,257:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 2 | PSO matches Adaptive but costs 14x more runtime | Not practical for production |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,257:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 3 | Neural estimator = LS
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,259:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (no learning occurred) | Needs retraining or architectural changes |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,259:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 4 | JIDD-SCMA achieves zero BER above 9 dB
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Best for URLLC scenarios |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 5 | JIDD-SCMA had a critical N0-overflow bug | Fixed; needs numerical guards |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 6 |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 64-QAM BER floor is 37x worse than QPSK | Higher modulation needs better estimation |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,263:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 7 | TR 38.901 is hardest
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: channel (BER floor ~3e-4) | Realistic factory scenario |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 8 | Rayleigh/Rician achieve zero BER at high SNR | LDPC
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coding is not the bottleneck |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 9 | Large factory BER ~0.21 at all SNR | System is fundamentally broken at this scale
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 10 | DFT is worst estimator (BER ~8e-3) | May improve on small factory (needs retest) |
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. Suggested Next Steps
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: High Priority
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fix the Neural estimator.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  It currently produces identical results to LS, wasting computational
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: resources. Suggested actions:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Train on more diverse channel realizations (multiple SNR points, factory sizes)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,271:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Increase model capacity or try a different architecture (e.g., attention-based)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,271:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Use curriculum learning starting from easy channels (Rayleigh) to hard (TR 38.901)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Solve the large factory problem.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  BER of 0.21 is unusable. Potential approaches:
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Increase BS antennas from 8 to 16 or 32
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Implement user scheduling to serve subsets of the 16 UTs per frame
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Deploy distributed MIMO with multiple access points
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Test with Adaptive estimator (may help but unlikely to solve the fundamental
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: under-determined problem)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,276:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Run Adaptive estimator on higher-order modulation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,278:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The 64-QAM BER floor with LS (1.1e-2)
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,279:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: may improve 10x with Adaptive estimation. This would validate whether Adaptive + 64-QAM is
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,280:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: viable for high-throughput factory applications.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,280:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Medium Priority
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,280:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,281:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Re-run DFT on small factory.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,283:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The current comparison is unfair since DFT was tested on the
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,283:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: medium factory while all others used small. A fair comparison would clarify whether DFT
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,283:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,284:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s poor
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,284:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: performance is inherent or an artifact of the test configuration.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,285:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,285:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Test Adaptive estimator on Rayleigh/Rician channels.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,288:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  LS already achieves zero BER on
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,289:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rayleigh above 8 dB. Adaptive could potentially reach zero BER at even lower SNR (4-6 dB),
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,289:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: demonstrating its value across channel types.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,290:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,290:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Run resource manager benchmarks.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,294:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Only archived data from earlier runs (March 5-14) exists for
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the 7 resource managers (Static, Round Robin, Max Throughput, PF, WMMSE, Queue-Aware,
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DRL). Fresh runs with the current configuration would provide up-to-date comparisons.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Research Directions
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  7 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Integrate JIDD-SCMA with Adaptive estimation.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,300:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Currently JIDD uses MMSE channel
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,300:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimation. Replacing it with the Adaptive estimator could push the waterfall region to even lower
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,301:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SNR.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,301:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  8 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,301:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Investigate iterative channel estimation with decoder feedback.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,305:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The persistent BER floor across
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,308:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: all OFDM estimators suggests that pilot-only estimation has fundamental limits. Feeding soft
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,309:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: decoder output back to refine channel estimates (turbo equalization) could break through this floor.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,309:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  9 
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,309:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Add numerical stability guards to JIDD-SCMA.
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,311:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  The N0-overflow bug in Run 1 should be
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,312:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: permanently guarded against with clamping in the log-likelihood computation to prevent future
   DEBUG: 2026-03-27 09:30:21,312:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: regressions.
